From 24c3eda1034ba6447bfe6263e4f04de11a255362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:46:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(backend): stop a Desktop wake burst queueing on the
 config parse and the ledger rebuild [daveey]

A wake burst (/api/sessions/<id>, /api/session-kanban-tasks, kanban boards,
profiles sessions, /api/status at once) ran 6-9 s on a loaded Mac and tripped
the Desktop's 5 s timeouts. py-spy on a hub backend under the same burst:

- /api/status parsed the ~2500-line config.yaml on every call for the
  _config_version stamp (~40 ms of GIL-held YAML each, 101 samples/burst).
  read_config_version_stamp now caches the parse on the file signature;
  parse errors still re-read, warn and raise. -> 5 samples/burst.
- /api/session-kanban-tasks asks for stale_ok, but in links_reader=replica
  mode replica_cards -> _ledger_owners called _remote_links() without it, so
  the strip waited on _links_lock for every ledger rebuild (any board write).
  stale_ok now reaches _ledger_owners. -> 143 -> 21 samples/burst.

Tests: test_config_version_stamp_cache.py (new), two stale_ok tests in
test_kanban_chat_links.py; red on the old code, green now.
---
